WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.202
Evaluation compares model predictions with the correct answers in the test set.

00:00:05.202 --> 00:00:09.557
Accuracy is the proportion of predictions that are correct.

00:00:09.557 --> 00:00:16.579
The confusion matrix gives more detail by separating correct and incorrect predictions for each class.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:20.956
Do not rely on accuracy alone in every problem.

00:00:20.956 --> 00:00:28.406
If one class is rare, a model can look accurate while still performing poorly on the cases that matter.

00:00:28.406 --> 00:00:35.488
For this introductory example, focus on understanding that evaluation must happen on unseen data.
